#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Kids OS Movies bridge: plays approved Plex movies on the chosen Roku TV.

Netflix titles can go on the list too: they open in the Netflix app on the
Roku (ECP deep link), in whichever Netflix profile was used last on that TV,
and get rewound to the start if Netflix resumes partway in.

Runs on the Linux host because Android (Waydroid) sits behind NAT and can't
discover TVs on the home network, and so the Plex account token never enters
the kid's Android. The Movies app talks to it over HTTP at the host's Waydroid
address (192.168.240.1:8766).

Kid endpoints (anyone on the Waydroid network):
  GET  /api/movies              approved movies
  GET  /api/poster/<key>        poster image
  POST /api/play/<key>          play from the beginning on the TV, if it's on
  POST /api/play-local/<key>    watch on the tablet instead (only while the TV is paused or
                                no TV is set up; "local" in /api/movies): picks a show's
                                episode, resets progress, returns the Plex key to open
  POST /api/dance-local/<id>    the same for a Dance song (the app opens YouTube Kids)
  GET  /api/theme               the logged-in kid's theme; POST /api/theme/<name> sets it
  GET  /api/dance               the Dance app's songs; GET /api/dance-thumb/<id> a picture
  POST /api/dance-play/<id,...> play the songs on the TV (YouTube), one after another
  GET  /api/coloring            the Paint app's coloring pages; GET /api/coloring-page/<id> one (PNG)
  GET  /api/allowed             may the logged-in kid use the tablet now (bedtime/limits)
  POST /api/activity?title=     the kid opened an app (for the parents' history)
Lists, schedules and history are per kid (the kidsos-kids group); kid routes use
the kid logged in on the screen, parent routes ?kid=<user> (default: the kid whose
tablet the parent last opened in parent mode, see POST /api/parent-kid/<user>).
Parent endpoints (only while the parent is logged in on the desktop, or from
the host itself):
  GET  /api/setup               current settings
  POST /api/link                start linking a Plex account (returns a code)
  GET  /api/link                has the code been entered yet?
  GET  /api/profiles            Plex Home profiles
  POST /api/profile/<id>        use this profile for playback
  GET  /api/tvs                 Roku TVs on the network
  POST /api/tv/<serial>         use this TV
  GET  /api/library?q=          movies the profile can see
  POST/DELETE /api/movies/<key> add/remove an approved movie
  POST /api/netflix/<id>        add a Netflix title (the number in its netflix.com/title/ link)
  POST /api/portal-pin          set the web portal PIN ({"pin": "1234"})
  GET  /api/themes              everyone's theme; POST /api/themes/<user>/<name> sets one
Web portal for the parents' phones (home network only, PIN-protected):
  GET  /                        the portal page
  POST /api/portal/login        {"pin": ...}; sets a session cookie
  GET  /api/portal/status       pause state and the approved list
  POST /api/portal/pause        {"minutes": n | "tomorrow" | "forever" | 0 (resume)}
  GET  /api/portal/library?q=   search, POST/DELETE /api/portal/items/<key>
  POST /api/portal/netflix      {"ref": "<netflix.com/title/... link or its number>"}
  GET/POST /api/portal/volume   the kid volume ({"percent": 0-100}), via tablet-volume
  GET  /api/portal/kids         the kids; lists, schedule and history routes take ?kid=
  GET/POST /api/portal/schedule allowed hours, daily limit; POST extra, sleep (?kid=)
  GET  /api/portal/history      what the kid played and opened; GET now, POST tv-stop
  GET  /api/portal/system       TV, Plex, last update, disk space, uptime
  GET  /api/portal/dance        the Dance songs; POST/DELETE /api/portal/dance/<id>
  GET  /api/portal/dance-library?q=  Danny Go! songs; POST /api/portal/dance-link {"ref"}
  GET  /api/portal/week         the last 7 days: minutes per day, top shows and apps (?kid=)
  GET  /api/portal/coloring     the coloring pages; GET coloring-search?q= (Openclipart),
                                POST/DELETE /api/portal/coloring/<id> ({"title"}) add/remove,
                                POST coloring-url {"url", "title"}, POST coloring-upload?title=
                                (the picture file as the body)
"""
